Kaggriculture Reference Agents -- licensing notice
=================================================

WHAT IS LICENSED HOW
--------------------

  *.py                  MIT (see LICENSE)
  *.csv, description    CC BY-SA 4.0

The .py files were originally published under CC BY-SA 4.0. That was a mistake for
code, for two reasons. No Creative Commons licence except CC0 is OSI-approved, and
Kaggriculture's rules require that open source code used to build a submission be under
an OSI-approved licence. More importantly, ShareAlike is copyleft: building a submission
on a BY-SA file arguably obliges you to license the adapted work BY-SA, which then
collides with that same requirement. Creative Commons themselves advise against using CC
licences for software.

The MIT grant is in addition to the earlier one, not instead of it. CC BY-SA 4.0 is
irrevocable, so anyone who took these files under it keeps that option; MIT simply
removes the obstacle for anyone building a submission.

SCOPE -- PLEASE READ IF YOU ARE REUSING TIERS 6-9
-------------------------------------------------

Tiers 0-5 (fallow_finn, wheat_walter, rotation_rosa, homestead_hana, melon_mateo,
rancher_rita) are original work by the dataset author and are MIT in full.

Tiers 6-9 (broker_bea, ledger_lena, slotter_silas, closer_cleo) are not entirely the
author's work, and the MIT grant is correspondingly narrower. What is covered: the
market/SELL layer, the scheduler, and everything else written around the plan. What is
NOT covered: the base85-encoded `_TRACE` field plan each of those files embeds.

That plan is the shared public meta line, not anyone's original contribution.
Running scripts/cross_team_identity.py over 530 downloaded public replays finds identical
712-turn farmer/hand sequences played by large groups of unrelated teams -- one group of
29 teams, another of 15, another of 8, with 104 distinct teams appearing in at least one
shared plan. No individual team is credited because the line demonstrably belongs to
none of them, and the author will not claim a licence over it either. It is reconstructible
from public replay data by anyone who wants it, and it reaches you on whatever terms the
competition's own rules provide.

If that ambiguity matters for your use, build on tiers 0-5. They are the documented
teaching ladder, and they are unambiguously yours to use.

THE ENVIRONMENT
---------------

Every measurement in this dataset was produced with kaggle-environments 1.32.7
(Apache-2.0), https://github.com/Kaggle/kaggle-environments. The agents restate small
factual tables from that environment (crop costs, animal yields, price-curve parameters)
so that each file is dependency-free.
